    "question": "A coil spring with the spring constant $85\\ \\mathrm{N/m}$ is stretched $12\\ \\mathrm{cm}$. How large is the pulling force?",
    "answer": {
     "value": 10.2,
     "unit": "N"
    },
    "solution": "Hooke's law gives the force directly:\n\n$$ F = k \\cdot \\Delta l $$\n\nGiven values:\n$$\n\\left[ \\begin{array}{l}\nk = 85\\ \\mathrm{N/m} \\\\\n\\Delta l = 12\\ \\mathrm{cm} = 0.12\\ \\mathrm{m}\n\\end{array} \\right]\n$$\n\n$$ F = 85 \\cdot 0.12 = 10.2\\ \\mathrm{N} $$\n\n**Answer:** The force is about $10\\ \\mathrm{N}$.\n\n**General conclusion:** Remember that the extension must be in metres when the spring constant is in N/m. Convert to SI units first, then substitute."
