    "solution": "We solve for the extension in Hooke's law:\n\n$$ F = k \\cdot \\Delta l \\quad\\Leftrightarrow\\quad \\Delta l = \\frac{F}{k} $$\n\nGiven values:\n$$\n\\left[ \\begin{array}{l}\nF = 24\\ \\mathrm{N} \\\\\nk = 150\\ \\mathrm{N/m}\n\\end{array} \\right]\n$$\n\n$$ \\Delta l = \\frac{24}{150} = 0.16\\ \\mathrm{m} = 16\\ \\mathrm{cm} $$\n\n**Answer:** The spring is stretched $0.16\\ \\mathrm{m}$ (= $16\\ \\mathrm{cm}$)."
