    "answer": {
     "value": 0.098,
     "unit": "J"
    },
    "solution": "The difference in oscillation energy between the turning points corresponds to the energy converted into heat.\n\n$$ E_\\text{heat} = E_1 - E_3 = \\frac{k \\cdot A_1^2}{2} - \\frac{k \\cdot A_3^2}{2} = \\frac{k}{2}(A_1^2 - A_3^2) $$\n\nGiven values:\n$$\n\\left[ \\begin{array}{l}\nk = 35\\ \\mathrm{N/m} \\\\\nA_1 = 9.0\\ \\mathrm{cm} = 0.090\\ \\mathrm{m} \\\\\nA_3 = 5.0\\ \\mathrm{cm} = 0.050\\ \\mathrm{m}\n\\end{array} \\right]\n$$\n\n$$ E_1 = \\frac{35 \\cdot 0.090^2}{2} = 0.14175\\ \\mathrm{J} $$\n\n$$ E_3 = \\frac{35 \\cdot 0.050^2}{2} = 0.04375\\ \\mathrm{J} $$\n\n$$ E_\\text{heat} = 0.14175 - 0.04375 = 0.098\\ \\mathrm{J} $$\n\n**Answer:** About $0.098\\ \\mathrm{J}$ has been converted into heat.\n\n**General conclusion:** In a damped oscillation the amplitude decreases over time, and the energy loss is not linear in the amplitude: since *E* ∝ *A*² the loss is distributed quadratically."
