   {
    "level": 2,
    "question": "A weight is hung from a spring with the spring constant $50\\ \\mathrm{N/m}$ and extends it $12\\ \\mathrm{cm}$. The same weight is then hung from two such springs connected in series. How much is the pair of springs extended?",
    "answer": {
     "value": 0.24,
     "unit": "m"
    },
    "solution": "The weight is the same in both cases, so the force on the springs is the same. We find it from the first extension using Hooke's law:\n\n$$ F = k \\cdot \\Delta l = 50 \\cdot 0.12 = 6.0\\ \\mathrm{N} $$\n\nFor $n$ identical springs in series, $k_\\mathrm{R} = \\dfrac{k}{n}$. Here $n = 2$:\n\n$$ k_\\mathrm{R} = \\frac{k}{n} = \\frac{50}{2} = 25\\ \\mathrm{N/m} $$\n\nHooke's law for the pair gives the extension:\n\n$$ F = k_\\mathrm{R} \\cdot \\Delta l \\quad\\Leftrightarrow\\quad \\Delta l = \\frac{F}{k_\\mathrm{R}} $$\n\nGiven values:\n$$\n\\left[ \\begin{array}{l}\nF = 6.0\\ \\mathrm{N} \\\\\nk_\\mathrm{R} = 25\\ \\mathrm{N/m}\n\\end{array} \\right]\n$$\n\n$$ \\Delta l = \\frac{6.0}{25} = 0.24\\ \\mathrm{m} $$\n\n**Answer:** The pair of springs is extended $0.24\\ \\mathrm{m}$, that is $24\\ \\mathrm{cm}$.\n\n**General conclusion:** In series each spring carries the whole weight and is extended as much as it would be on its own. Two identical springs therefore give twice the extension."
   },
   {
    "level": 3,
    "question": "A bow is drawn $32\\ \\mathrm{cm}$ with a tension of $180\\ \\mathrm{N}$. The arrow is shot horizontally from a height of $1.6\\ \\mathrm{m}$ above the ground and lands $24\\ \\mathrm{m}$ away. Determine the mass of the arrow. Use $g = 9.82\\ \\mathrm{m/s^2}$ and ignore air resistance.\n\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 480.0 230.0\" style=\"max-width:480px;width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:16px auto;background:#fff;border:1px solid rgba(15,22,32,0.12);border-radius:6px;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif\"><rect x=\"58\" y=\"34\" width=\"50\" height=\"150\" fill=\"rgba(15,22,32,0.06)\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"36\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"440\" y2=\"184\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"42\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"35\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"54\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"47\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"66\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"59\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"78\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"71\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"90\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"83\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"102\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"95\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"114\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"107\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"126\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"119\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"138\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"131\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"143\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"162\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"155\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"174\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"167\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"186\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"179\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"198\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"191\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"210\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"203\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"222\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"215\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"234\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"227\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"246\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"239\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"258\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"251\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"270\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"263\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"282\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"275\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"294\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"287\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"306\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"299\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"318\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"311\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"323\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"342\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"335\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"354\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"347\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"366\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"359\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"378\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"371\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"390\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"383\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"402\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"414\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"407\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"426\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"419\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"438\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"431\" y2=\"192\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M 108.0 34.0 L 118.7 34.2 L 129.5 34.7 L 140.2 35.5 L 150.9 36.7 L 161.7 38.2 L 172.4 40.0 L 183.1 42.2 L 193.9 44.7 L 204.6 47.5 L 215.3 50.7 L 226.1 54.2 L 236.8 58.0 L 247.5 62.2 L 258.3 66.7 L 269.0 71.5 L 279.7 76.7 L 290.5 82.2 L 301.2 88.0 L 311.9 94.2 L 322.7 100.7 L 333.4 107.5 L 344.1 114.7 L 354.9 122.2 L 365.6 130.0 L 376.3 138.2 L 387.1 146.7 L 397.8 155.5 L 408.5 164.7 L 419.3 174.2 L 430.0 184.0\" stroke=\"#c8324a\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/><circle cx=\"108\" cy=\"34\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#0f1620\"/><line x1=\"114.0\" y1=\"34.0\" x2=\"162.0\" y2=\"34.0\" stroke=\"#c8324a\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"162.0,34.0 153.9,37.9 153.9,30.1\" fill=\"#c8324a\"/><circle cx=\"430.0\" cy=\"184\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#c8324a\"/></svg>",
    "answer": {
     "value": 0.033,
     "unit": "kg"
    },
    "solution": "The task combines **spring energy**, **energy conversion** and **horizontal projection**.\n\n**Step 1: the launch speed of the arrow from the projectile calculation.** The height of fall gives the time of fall via $h = \\dfrac{1}{2}gt^2$:\n\n$$ t = \\sqrt{\\frac{2h}{g}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\cdot 1.6}{9.82}} = 0.5712\\ \\mathrm{s} $$\n\nDuring that time the arrow travels the distance *x* horizontally at constant speed $v_0$:\n\n$$ v_0 = \\frac{x}{t} = \\frac{24}{0.5712} = 42.02\\ \\mathrm{m/s} $$\n\n**Step 2: the energy stored in the drawn bow.** By Hooke's law the spring constant is $k = F/A = 180/0.32 = 562.5\\ \\mathrm{N/m}$. The stored energy is\n\n$$ E = \\frac{k \\cdot A^2}{2} = \\frac{562.5 \\cdot 0.32^2}{2} = 28.8\\ \\mathrm{J} $$\n\n(Alternative: the triangle area $E = \\dfrac{1}{2}FA = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\cdot 180\\cdot 0.32 = 28.8\\ \\mathrm{J}$.)\n\n**Step 3: the principle of conservation of energy.** All the stored energy is converted into the kinetic energy of the arrow:\n\n$$ E = \\frac{m \\cdot v_0^2}{2} \\quad\\Leftrightarrow\\quad m = \\frac{2E}{v_0^2} $$\n\nGiven values:\n$$\n\\left[ \\begin{array}{l}\nE = 28.8\\ \\mathrm{J} \\\\\nv_0 = 42.02\\ \\mathrm{m/s}\n\\end{array} \\right]\n$$\n\n$$ m = \\frac{2 \\cdot 28.8}{42.02^2} = \\frac{57.6}{1766} \\approx 0.0326\\ \\mathrm{kg} $$\n\n**Answer:** The arrow has a mass of about $33\\ \\mathrm{g}$.\n\n**General conclusion:** Three different parts must fall into place: (1) the projectile calculation gives the launch speed of the arrow, (2) Hooke's law (or the triangle area) gives the stored energy, (3) the principle of conservation of energy links them. Seeing *which three principles* belong to the same task is the whole step up in level."
   }
