    "solution": "The maximum acceleration in a harmonic oscillation is\n\n$$ a_{\\max} = \\omega^2 \\cdot A $$\n\nGiven values:\n$$\n\\left[ \\begin{array}{l}\n\\omega = 20\\ \\mathrm{rad/s} \\\\\nA = 0.050\\ \\mathrm{m}\n\\end{array} \\right]\n$$\n\n$$ a_{\\max} = 20^2 \\cdot 0.050 = 400 \\cdot 0.050 = 20\\ \\mathrm{m/s^2} $$\n\n**Answer:** The maximum acceleration is $20\\ \\mathrm{m/s^2}$.\n\n**General conclusion:** The maximum acceleration is reached at the turning points (the peaks and bottoms of the curve), where the resultant force is largest. At the equilibrium position the acceleration is 0."
