    "solution": "We solve for the spring constant:\n\n$$ T = 2\\pi\\sqrt{\\frac{m}{k}} \\quad\\Leftrightarrow\\quad k = \\frac{4\\pi^2 \\cdot m}{T^2} $$\n\nGiven values:\n$$\n\\left[ \\begin{array}{l}\nm = 0.40\\ \\mathrm{kg} \\\\\nT = 1.2\\ \\mathrm{s}\n\\end{array} \\right]\n$$\n\n$$ k = \\frac{4\\pi^2 \\cdot 0.40}{1.2^2} = \\frac{15.79}{1.44} \\approx 11\\ \\mathrm{N/m} $$\n\n**Answer:** The spring constant is about $11\\ \\mathrm{N/m}$."
