    "answer": {
     "value": 2.84,
     "unit": "s"
    },
    "solution": "The period of a simple pendulum is given by\n\n$$ T = 2\\pi\\sqrt{\\frac{l}{g}} $$\n\nGiven values:\n$$\n\\left[ \\begin{array}{l}\nl = 2.0\\ \\mathrm{m} \\\\\ng \\approx 9.82\\ \\mathrm{m/s^2}\n\\end{array} \\right]\n$$\n\n$$ T = 2\\pi\\sqrt{\\frac{2.0}{9.82}} = 2\\pi\\cdot 0.4514 \\approx 2.84\\ \\mathrm{s} $$\n\n**Answer:** The period is about $2.8\\ \\mathrm{s}$.\n\n**General conclusion:** The mass of the pendulum plays no role; only the length and the gravitational acceleration do."
