    "solution": "We solve for the length of the pendulum in the period formula:\n\n$$ T = 2\\pi\\sqrt{\\frac{l}{g}} \\quad\\Leftrightarrow\\quad T^2 = 4\\pi^2 \\cdot \\frac{l}{g} \\quad\\Leftrightarrow\\quad l = \\frac{T^2 \\cdot g}{4\\pi^2} $$\n\nGiven values:\n$$\n\\left[ \\begin{array}{l}\nT = 1.50\\ \\mathrm{s} \\\\\ng \\approx 9.82\\ \\mathrm{m/s^2}\n\\end{array} \\right]\n$$\n\n$$ l = \\frac{1.50^2 \\cdot 9.82}{4\\pi^2} = \\frac{22.10}{39.48} \\approx 0.56\\ \\mathrm{m} $$\n\n**Answer:** The length of the pendulum is about $0.56\\ \\mathrm{m}$."
