    "question": "An astronaut takes a simple pendulum with a length of $0.30\\ \\mathrm{m}$ to an alien planet. There the pendulum is measured to have the period $1.20\\ \\mathrm{s}$. Determine the gravitational acceleration on the planet.\n\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 360.0 231.0\" style=\"max-width:360px;width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:16px auto;background:#fff;border:1px solid rgba(15,22,32,0.12);border-radius:6px;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif\"><line x1=\"117.20000000000002\" y1=\"26\" x2=\"257.20000000000005\" y2=\"26\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"123.20000000000002\" y1=\"26\" x2=\"116.20000000000002\" y2=\"18\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"135.20000000000002\" y1=\"26\" x2=\"128.20000000000002\" y2=\"18\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"147.20000000000002\" y1=\"26\" x2=\"140.20000000000002\" y2=\"18\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"159.20000000000002\" y1=\"26\" x2=\"152.20000000000002\" y2=\"18\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"171.20000000000002\" y1=\"26\" x2=\"164.20000000000002\" y2=\"18\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"183.20000000000002\" y1=\"26\" x2=\"176.20000000000002\" y2=\"18\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"195.20000000000002\" y1=\"26\" x2=\"188.20000000000002\" y2=\"18\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"207.20000000000002\" y1=\"26\" x2=\"200.20000000000002\" y2=\"18\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"219.20000000000002\" y1=\"26\" x2=\"212.20000000000002\" y2=\"18\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"231.20000000000002\" y1=\"26\" x2=\"224.20000000000002\" y2=\"18\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"243.20000000000002\" y1=\"26\" x2=\"236.20000000000002\" y2=\"18\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"255.20000000000002\" y1=\"26\" x2=\"248.20000000000002\" y2=\"18\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"187.20000000000002\" cy=\"26\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#0f1620\"/><path d=\"M 144.9 195.8 A 175 175 0 0 0 229.5 195.8\" stroke=\"#8a8579\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><line x1=\"187.20000000000002\" y1=\"26\" x2=\"144.9\" y2=\"195.8\" stroke=\"#8a8579\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><circle cx=\"144.9\" cy=\"195.8\" r=\"8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><line x1=\"187.20000000000002\" y1=\"26\" x2=\"187.20000000000002\" y2=\"201\" stroke=\"#0f1620\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><circle cx=\"187.20000000000002\" cy=\"201\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#0f1620\"/><text x=\"178.2\" y=\"113.5\" font-family=\"Poppins,sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#0f1620\" text-anchor=\"end\" dominant-baseline=\"middle\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" paint-order=\"stroke\"><tspan font-style=\"italic\">l</tspan> = 0.30 m</text></svg>",
    "answer": {
     "value": 8.22,
     "unit": "m/s²"
    },
    "solution": "We solve for the gravitational acceleration:\n\n$$ T = 2\\pi\\sqrt{\\frac{l}{g}} \\quad\\Leftrightarrow\\quad g = \\frac{4\\pi^2 \\cdot l}{T^2} $$\n\nGiven values:\n$$\n\\left[ \\begin{array}{l}\nl = 0.30\\ \\mathrm{m} \\\\\nT = 1.20\\ \\mathrm{s}\n\\end{array} \\right]\n$$\n\n$$ g = \\frac{4\\pi^2 \\cdot 0.30}{1.20^2} = \\frac{11.84}{1.44} \\approx 8.2\\ \\mathrm{m/s^2} $$\n\n**Answer:** The gravitational acceleration on the planet is about $8.2\\ \\mathrm{m/s^2}$.\n\n**General conclusion:** A simple pendulum is a simple instrument for measuring the gravitational acceleration: the period gives *g* directly, since the length of the pendulum is easily measured with a tape measure."
