    "level": 1,
    "question": "An oscillation has the period $0.025\\ \\mathrm{s}$. Determine the frequency.",
    "answer": {
     "value": 40,
     "unit": "Hz"
    },
    "solution": "The natural frequency is the inverse of the period:\n\n$$ f = \\frac{1}{T} $$\n\nGiven values:\n$$\n\\left[ \\begin{array}{l}\nT = 0.025\\ \\mathrm{s}\n\\end{array} \\right]\n$$\n\n$$ f = \\frac{1}{0.025} = 40\\ \\mathrm{Hz} $$\n\n**Answer:** The frequency is $40\\ \\mathrm{Hz}$.\n\n**General conclusion:** $1\\ \\mathrm{Hz} = 1$ oscillation per second. A frequency of $40\\ \\mathrm{Hz}$ is at the bottom of the audible range (typical bass)."
