    "solution": "In an open pipe both ends are antinodes. The fundamental ($n = 1$) has a node in the middle, so the length of the pipe corresponds to half a wavelength:\n\n$$ l = \\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\quad\\Leftrightarrow\\quad \\lambda = 2l $$\n\nGiven values:\n$$\n\\left[ \\begin{array}{l}\nl = 0.40\\ \\mathrm{m} \\\\\nv = 340\\ \\mathrm{m/s}\n\\end{array} \\right]\n$$\n\n$$ \\lambda = 2 \\cdot 0.40 = 0.80\\ \\mathrm{m} $$\n\n$$ f = \\frac{v}{\\lambda} = \\frac{340}{0.80} = 425\\ \\mathrm{Hz} $$\n\n**Answer:** The frequency of the fundamental is $425\\ \\mathrm{Hz}$."
