    "solution": "We first need the wave speed in deep water, then the angle of refraction.\n\n**Step 1: wave speed in deep water.**\n\n$$ v_1 = f \\cdot \\lambda_1 = 0.50 \\cdot 6.0 = 3.0\\ \\mathrm{m/s} $$\n\n**Step 2: the angle of refraction.**\n\n$$ \\sin b = \\frac{v_2}{v_1}\\sin i = \\frac{1.5}{3.0}\\cdot\\sin 45^\\circ = 0.5 \\cdot 0.7071 = 0.3536 $$\n\n$$ b = \\sin^{-1}(0.3536) \\approx 20.7^\\circ $$\n\n**Answer:** The angle of refraction is about $21^\\circ$.\n\n**General conclusion:** When the wave slows down (here the speed is halved) it is refracted towards the normal: a typical case that happens when waves approach the shore."
